# usher/replay: commands a terminal may be restarted running.
#
# One per line, as you would type it. A terminal whose foreground job is a
# listed command is remembered apart from an idle shell in the same
# directory, and at the next login it comes back running that command,
# inside a shell that stays when the command ends.
#
# OPT-IN, PER COMMAND. Re-running something you typed is a different act from
# starting an app out of its desktop entry: `top` is harmless, `make deploy`
# is not. Anything not listed here comes back as a plain shell in its
# directory. A script run by a shell is matched by its own name.
top
htop
btop
